  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In December 2022, the Government of Botswana, after consultation with the social partners, deposited the instruments for the ratification of two governance Convention: The Labour Inspection Convention, C.181 and the Labour Inspection (Agriculture) Convention, C.129.

During the 2024-2025 ILO programme cycle  ILO support twill focus on ensuring reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
